<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11155" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀορτ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀείρω</span>) in pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρόγχια</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Loc.Hom.</u>
				14
			</span></i> (where Littré reads <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀορτρέων, -τρῃσι</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Coac.</u>
				394
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ruf.
				<u>Onom.</u>
				159
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> the
				<i>arteries</i> springing from the heart, i.e. aorta and
			pulmonary artery, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Cord.</u>
				10
			</span></i>; esp. in sg., the <i>aorta,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				496a7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				513b4
			</span></i>, etc.: in pl., <i>arteries,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.205
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>knapsack that hung from</i> the shoulders, <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				331
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.
				40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
				10
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.79
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.139
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>point of suspension</i> of a balance, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
				29
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
